<BaseLayout title="About — Priyanga P Kini" description="Engineer at nilenso, working on distributed and analytical systems at scale.">
  <section class="intro intro-large">
    <h1 class="page-title">About <span class="title-accent">me</span></h1>
    <p>I build software for a living. I am also a member of <a href="https://nilenso.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link">nilenso</a>, a tech cooperative where we are building a new standard for tech consulting.</p>
    <p>Through nilenso, I have worked on distributed and analytical systems at scale. At Resolve To Save Lives, I built the backend powering an analytics dashboard over 6M+ patient records, and migrated product workflows to open standards like DHIS2 and OpenSRP.</p>
    <p>At Porter, I built a Temporal-based driver onboarding workflow, migrated high-throughput APIs from a legacy Ruby-based Order Management System (OMS) to modern Kotlin services with a 3x performance improvement, and developed a Google Gemini-based OCR solution with ~90% accuracy for document verification at a 10x cost reduction.</p>
    <p>Most recently, I co-developed <a href="https://github.com/nilenso/megasthenes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link">Megasthenes</a>, an open-source TypeScript SDK for question-answering over code repositories using LLM-powered agents.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
